ture | The gateway keys instance-scoped stop flags and rate limits on an unverified caller header, and the approval resume starts a new trace. | Bind the instance to a verified claim (or drop instance-scoped decisions in the gateway), and store and restore traceparent with each approval grant. | [('src/gateway.py', 170)] ['Assign instance and tenant identity in the trusted execution layer.'] False False\nA05 gap G1 operations | Stopping one agent type is not enforced at the gateway, and gateway audit rows carry only caller-supplied type and instance IDs. | Add agent_type to the gateway stop query using a token-bound ID, and record verified IDs in gateway audit rows. | [('migrations/001_init.sql', 23)] ['contain the right instance or agent type'] False False\nC01 gap G2 agent_team | The release manifest omits issuer/audience bindings and other required categories, and most artifacts lack an owner and immutable reference. | Add issuer/audience, MCP protocol, tool-fingerprint and cache settings; add owner and digest or commit for each artifact. | [('src/main.py', 36)] ['issuer/audience bindings'] False False\nC02 gap G2 governance | A catch-all CODEOWNERS entry lets one team change Dockerfile, dependencies and most of src/, and no emergency-change path is in the repo. | Give Dockerfile, requirements.txt and src/ named owners including security; document an emergency change path. | [('CODEOWNERS', 1)] ['Show who is allowed to change production config'] False False\nC03 gap G1 infrastructure | Only the agent checks its own identity at start-up; no process outside it compares the running prompt, model and tool setup to the approved manifest. | Add an external check, such as an admission rule or scheduled job, that compares observed pod artifacts with release/manifest.yaml. | [('k8s/admission.yaml', 41)] ['Check the running setup against the approved manifest'] False False\nC04 gap G2 operations | No drift check compares running prompts, tools, permissions or network policy with the approved baseline. | Add a scheduled per-deployment drift job with alert, response and time limit set in config. | [('k8s/admission.yaml', 22)] ['Compare running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against their approved baseline'] False False\nC05 gap G2 agent_team | Dependencies and model are pinned, but no scheduled re-testing or provider-notice watch exists for the hosted model. | Add a scheduled job that re-runs the release suite against the pinned model and tracks provider version notices. | [('release/manifest.yaml', 45)] ['Keep scheduled re-testing'] False False\nC06 gap G2 agent_team | The release workflow runs a test path that does not exist and stores no results tied to the candidate manifest. | Add tests/release with the required attack and allowed-task cases, run them against the built digest, and upload results tagged with the manifest digest. | [('.github/workflows/release.yml', 29)] ['Keep the results for the exact candidate manifest'] False False\nC07 gap G2 operations | No approved recovery setup or rollback procedure exists, and the hosted model has no recorded retirement date. | Add a pinned recovery manifest, a tested rollback pipeline, and the model retirement date. | [('.github/workflows/release.yml', 75)] ['Keep an approved recovery setup and show that rollback works'] False False\nC08 gap G2 operations | Traces cannot be tied to a stored release manifest, and audit rows are kept about 6 weeks instead of six months. | Key a stored manifest by agent-type-id, make the gateway log a verified id, and set audit retention to the full audit period. | [('src/gateway.py', 138)] ['look up the release manifest', 'Keep these links for the full audit retention period'] False False\nE01 gap G2 governance | No inventory covers the gateway, STS, registry, audit and stop services, and entries name only one owner. | Create an inventory of every outside service with an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner. | [('release/manifest.yaml', 53)] ['name the owner on the agent team and the owner on the shared platform or vendor side', 'List the outside tools, MCP servers'] False False\nE02 gap G2 security | No vulnerability scan runs in CI and no dependency approval records exist. | Add a failing pip-audit step on requirements.txt and record publisher, permissions and update source per dependency. | [('.github/workflows/release.yml', 28)] ['known vulnerabilities', 'Record the limits of remote services and unsigned artifacts'] False False\nE03 gap G2 infrastructure | Fingerprints are re-checked only every 300s, list_changed is ignored, and a gateway 503 bypasses the block through the direct route. | Remove direct_route fallback, re-check on list_changed and each load, and record an implementation reference per server. | [('config/tools.yaml', 8)] ['Compare it whenever the tool loads, its cache refreshes, or its tool list changes', 'Block unexpected changes until reviewed, including when re-checking fails'] False False\nE04 gap G2 security | N/A claim was not upheld: Agent loads external HRIS/helpdesk MCP servers, so N/A does not hold; no metadata scanner exists. | Resolve the challenged feature or exposure and verify the applicable controls. | [('src/tools.py', 78)] ['scan server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates', 'Before the model sees them', \"Before the model sees them, scan server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates. Look for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and places data could be sent. Limit lengths, and clean or reject anything suspicious. Check that a scanner error doesn't quietly let unchecked metadata through.\"] False False\nE05 gap G2 infrastructure | Lookalike