 over the image digest, model record and every file in src, prompts and config plus requirements and Dockerfile. | Run the A03 recipe: hash a frozen manifest twice, then change each input one at a time. | [('src/type_id.py', 42)] ['Compute the agent-type-id as a hash of the container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, and configuration. The model part includes checkpoint and fine-tune or adapter references where they apply. Keep the list of inputs (the manifest) and the hashing steps. Check that changing any input changes the ID, and that the same manifest gives the same ID.'] False False\nA04 gap G1 infrastructure | The gateway keys instance-scoped stop flags and rate limits on an unverified caller header, and the approval resume starts a new trace. | Bind the instance to a verified claim (or drop instance-scoped decisions in the gateway), and store and restore traceparent with each approval grant. | [('src/gateway.py', 170)] ['Assign instance and tenant identity in the trusted execution layer.'] False False\nA05 gap G1 operations | Stopping one agent type is not enforced at the gateway, and gateway audit rows carry only caller-supplied type and instance IDs. | Add agent_type to the gateway stop query using a token-bound ID, and record verified IDs in gateway audit rows. | [('migrations/001_init.sql', 23)] ['contain the right instance or agent type'] False False\nC01 gap G2 agent_team | The release manifest omits issuer/audience bindings and other required categories, and most artifacts lack an owner and immutable reference. | Add issuer/audience, MCP protocol, tool-fingerprint and cache settings; add owner and digest or commit for each artifact. | [('src/main.py', 36)] ['issuer/audience bindings'] False False\nC02 gap G2 governance | A catch-all CODEOWNERS entry lets one team change Dockerfile, dependencies and most of src/, and no emergency-change path is in the repo. | Give Dockerfile, requirements.txt and src/ named owners including security;