ry setup and show that rollback works'] False False\nC08 gap G2 operations | Traces cannot be tied to a stored release manifest, and audit rows are kept about 6 weeks instead of six months. | Key a stored manifest by agent-type-id, make the gateway log a verified id, and set audit retention to the full audit period. | [('src/gateway.py', 138)] ['look up the release manifest', 'Keep these links for the full audit retention period'] False False\nE01 gap G2 governance | No inventory covers the gateway, STS, registry, audit and stop services, and entries name only one owner. | Create an inventory of every outside service with an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner. | [('release/manifest.yaml', 53)] ['name the owner on the agent team and the owner on the shared platform or vendor side', 'List the outside tools, MCP servers'] False False\nE02 gap G2 security | No vulnerability scan runs in CI and no dependency approval records exist. | Add a failing pip-audit step on requirements.txt and record publisher, permissions and update source per dependency. | [('.github/workflows/release.yml', 28)] ['known vulnerabilities', 'Record the limits of remote services and unsigned artifacts'] False False\nE03 gap G2 infrastructure | Fingerprints are re-checked only every 300s, list_changed is ignored, and a gateway 503 bypasses the block through the direct route. | Remove direct_route fallback, re-check on list_changed and each load, and record an implementation reference per server. | [('config/tools.yaml', 8)] ['Compare it whenever the tool loads, its cache refreshes, or its tool list changes', 'Block unexpected changes until reviewed, including when re-checking fails'] False False\nE04 gap G2 security | N/A claim was not upheld: Agent loads external HRIS/helpdesk MCP servers, so N/A does not hold; no metadata scanner exists. | Resolve the challenged feature or exposure and verify the applicable controls. | [('src/tools.py', 78)] ['scan server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates', 'Before the model sees them', \"Before the model sees them, scan server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates. Look for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and places data could be sent. Limit lengths, and clean or reject anything suspicious. Check that a scanner error doesn't quietly let unchecked metadata through.\"] False False\nE05 gap G2 infrastructure | Lookalike and duplicate tool names across servers are only logged, not flagged or blocked, and homoglyph variants are not detected. | Make refresh_fingerprints raise a conflict that disables the tools, widen normalization to confusables, and bind approval to server identity. | [('src/gateway.py', 67)] ['Flag lookalike and duplicate names across servers'] False False\nE06 gap G2 infrastructure | escalate_to_human falls back to a direct helpdesk-mcp call when the gateway returns 503 or is unreachable, skipping gateway policy, stop flags and logging. | Delete direct_route from config/tools.yaml and the fallback in gateway_client.py; remove the agent-to-helpdesk-mcp egress rule in k8s/networkpolicy.yaml. | [('src/gateway_client.py', 52)] ['Required checks fail closed', 'a gateway or equivalent enforcement layer the agent cannot bypass'] False False\nE09 gap G1 operations | Stop sets a flag but issued 300 s tokens are not revoked, and the direct route skips the gateway stop check. | Remove direct_route so the gateway stop check always applies, shorten token lifetime to the stop time or revoke on stop, and record in-flight calls at stop. | [('src/credentials.py', 20)] ['It must revoke access as needed'] False False\nE10 gap G1 infrastructure | Gateway audit rows lack verified identity fields and trace, vendor IDs are not linked, and the direct route skips the gateway audit. | Make gateway log verified fields and the vendor receipt ID, drop direct_route, and write allow records before forwarding. | [('src/gateway.py', 137)] ['all six identity fields kept'] False False\nE11 gap G2 infrastructure | Audit retention is about six weeks rather than six months, there is no integrity or gap detection, and the gateway audits after acting. | Raise KEEP_PARTITIONS to cover six months, add sequence/hash and gap alerts, write gateway audit before forwarding. | [('k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml', 35)] ['Keep records long enough for investigations and for the law'] False False\nE12 needs_evidence G3 security | No checks apply from code; runbook, alert routing, fleet impact query and outside-reporting owner are not in this repo. | Run the E12 drill and keep the impact query, quarantine and revocation records, alert times and the named reporting decision-maker. Also note gateway stop query (gateway.py:99) ignores agent_type scope (see R11). | [] [] False False\n    1500\nagent.py\napprovals.py\naudit.py\nbudgets.py\ncredentials.py\ngateway_client.py\ngateway.py\nkillswitch.py\nmain.py\nredact.py\nretrieval.py\ntools.py\ntype_id.py\nvalidation.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TkxMgdmY6CykbC2wzsQzPZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
